1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:03,336
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:06,464
[tense music playing]

3
00:00:20,353 --> 00:00:21,730
[screaming]

4
00:00:21,813 --> 00:00:23,773
[shattering sound]

5
00:00:27,694 --> 00:00:29,779
[Diego] <i>I've been wanting</i>
<i>to give you this.</i>

6
00:00:30,905 --> 00:00:32,032
<i>I love you so much.</i>

7
00:00:32,115 --> 00:00:34,784
[Natalie] <i>I didn't save</i>
<i>your life for nothing.</i>

8
00:00:34,868 --> 00:00:37,620
<i>I was hoping you would like me back.</i>

9
00:00:38,204 --> 00:00:39,122
[Jepoy] <i>It meant nothing, right?</i>

10
00:00:39,205 --> 00:00:41,416
<i>I don't want to see you together.</i>

11
00:00:41,499 --> 00:00:43,710
<i>-Why not?</i>
<i>-Isn't it obvious?!</i>

12
00:00:43,793 --> 00:00:45,628
<i>Jepoy, I like you.</i>

13
00:00:45,712 --> 00:00:47,589
<i>-I'm sorry.</i>
<i>-Anna, wait! Anna!</i>

14
00:00:47,672 --> 00:00:50,759
<i>I will come back, and when I do,</i>

15
00:00:50,842 --> 00:00:52,761
<i>I'll come back with a vengeance!</i>

16
00:00:53,178 --> 00:00:54,846
[Anna] <i>You look a little</i>
<i>happier than usual.</i>

17
00:00:54,929 --> 00:00:56,639
[Arnaldo] <i>I think I saw an angel.</i>

18
00:00:56,723 --> 00:00:57,849
<i>Is she my brother's girlfriend?</i>

19
00:00:57,932 --> 00:00:59,142
[Anna] <i>I know they're getting there.</i>

20
00:00:59,225 --> 00:01:01,811
<i>She's our friend, Lily.</i>

21
00:01:01,895 --> 00:01:04,397
<i>If she's your friend,</i>
<i>can you introduce me to her?</i>

22
00:01:04,481 --> 00:01:05,523
[Jepoy] <i>This is dangerous.</i>

23
00:01:05,607 --> 00:01:08,234
<i>Arnaldo was crazy obsessed</i>
<i>with Ivy back then.</i>

24
00:01:08,318 --> 00:01:11,613
<i>What if his memories come back?</i>

25
00:01:11,696 --> 00:01:13,323
[Lily] <i>You're the one who texted me?</i>

26
00:01:13,406 --> 00:01:16,076
[Emilia] <i>And you're the one</i>
<i>investigating my mother,</i>

27
00:01:16,159 --> 00:01:18,870
<i>trying to connect her to Red Dragon.</i>

28
00:01:18,953 --> 00:01:20,997
<i>This is a clone of Mercedes' phone.</i>

29
00:01:21,081 --> 00:01:23,166
[Jepoy] <i>You can keep</i>
<i>track of all her calls</i>

30
00:01:23,249 --> 00:01:24,375
<i>and text messages from here.</i>

31
00:01:24,459 --> 00:01:25,335
[Camia] <i>It's confirmed.</i>

32
00:01:25,418 --> 00:01:27,921
<i>That's another piece of evidence</i>
<i>that will prove</i>

33
00:01:28,004 --> 00:01:30,715
<i>that Helena Montoya is Red Dragon.</i>

34
00:01:30,799 --> 00:01:32,967
[Lily] <i>The people of Poblacion</i>
<i>Ardiente will soon know</i>

35
00:01:33,051 --> 00:01:34,427
<i>that their supposed angel</i>

36
00:01:34,511 --> 00:01:37,430
<i>is actually a devil in disguise.</i>

37
00:01:37,514 --> 00:01:39,140
[doctor] <i>Sometimes, you just need</i>

38
00:01:39,224 --> 00:01:41,476
<i>to jump-start the patient's brain.</i>

39
00:01:41,559 --> 00:01:45,522
<i>By that, I mean images that'll</i>
<i>ignite an intense emotion.</i>

40
00:01:45,605 --> 00:01:47,941
[Julio] <i>I'll get you back, Arnaldo.</i>

41
00:01:48,024 --> 00:01:50,652
<i>You'll be the man you once were.</i>

42
00:01:50,735 --> 00:01:52,320
<i>I promise you that.</i>

43
00:02:00,787 --> 00:02:01,913
[Jepoy] I'll get that.

44
00:02:02,997 --> 00:02:04,040
I'll be right with you.

45
00:02:12,465 --> 00:02:15,176
Excuse us for a while. We'll just talk.

46
00:02:22,976 --> 00:02:24,394
Um, Arnaldo…

47
00:02:25,520 --> 00:02:28,106
I'm sorry I haven't
visited you in a while.

48
00:02:29,941 --> 00:02:33,027
I haven't been feeling very well recently.

49
00:02:34,612 --> 00:02:35,655
You've been sick?

50
00:02:35,738 --> 00:02:37,407
Are you all right now? Do you feel better?

51
00:02:37,824 --> 00:02:42,328
Yes, thank you. I'm slowly recovering.

52
00:02:43,955 --> 00:02:45,456
In fact…

53
00:02:46,166 --> 00:02:49,168
the doctors are surprised
at my speedy recovery.

54
00:02:50,545 --> 00:02:51,880
But what they don't know…

55
00:02:52,547 --> 00:02:55,341
is that I have a new secret weapon.

56
00:02:59,846 --> 00:03:01,890
This is my new secret weapon.

57
00:03:02,849 --> 00:03:05,018
The inspired word of God,

58
00:03:05,643 --> 00:03:06,519
the Bible.

59
00:03:07,687 --> 00:03:08,646
You know what?

60
00:03:09,230 --> 00:03:10,398
It's because of you…

61
00:03:12,775 --> 00:03:14,694
that I started reading this again.

62
00:03:16,654 --> 00:03:17,697
[chuckles]

63
00:03:18,865 --> 00:03:20,533
-Praise the Lord.
-[Julio laughs]

64
00:03:26,247 --> 00:03:27,665
Thank you, grandson.

65
00:03:28,750 --> 00:03:31,836
You know, you inspired me.

66
00:03:32,295 --> 00:03:34,047
This brought light into my life.

67
00:03:34,672 --> 00:03:36,925
Seems like karma has hit
the Ardientes hard.

68
00:03:37,383 --> 00:03:38,384
Look at Julio.

69
00:03:39,886 --> 00:03:41,471
[Jepoy] Looks like he's gone nuts.

70
00:03:42,764 --> 00:03:45,975
Maybe because his family is all broken up.

71
00:03:47,518 --> 00:03:50,063
Anna, don't forget.
That man in front of you?

72
00:03:51,189 --> 00:03:52,565
That's Julio Ardiente.

73
00:03:52,649 --> 00:03:54,275
Even Satan fears him.

74
00:03:55,026 --> 00:03:56,486
Everyone can change.

75
00:03:56,569 --> 00:03:58,613
Look at Arnaldo.

76
00:03:59,155 --> 00:04:00,156
Even you.

77
00:04:02,283 --> 00:04:03,284
Me?

78
00:04:04,410 --> 00:04:07,038
I'm glad you didn't hurt Arnaldo earlier.

79
00:04:09,457 --> 00:04:11,125
Only because you don't want me to.

80
00:04:16,881 --> 00:04:17,966
[Helena on voice recording]
<i>I've already settled</i>

81
00:04:18,049 --> 00:04:19,676
<i>my problem with Mr. Yi</i>

82
00:04:19,759 --> 00:04:22,303
<i>regarding the gun shipment.</i>

83
00:04:23,346 --> 00:04:25,223
[Mercedes] <i>I have one</i>
<i>other concern, Madam.</i>

84
00:04:25,306 --> 00:04:28,434
<i>Emilia says she wants</i>
<i>to get rid of someone.</i>

85
00:04:29,727 --> 00:04:31,437
[Helena] <i>Prioritize the shipment.</i>

86
00:04:32,313 --> 00:04:34,065
<i>And I will take care of my daughter.</i>

87
00:04:34,607 --> 00:04:37,110
See, Attorney? Heard all that?

88
00:04:38,695 --> 00:04:42,407
It's clear. That was
Helena Montoya's voice.

89
00:04:42,490 --> 00:04:45,076
This proves that she is Red Dragon.

90
00:04:45,785 --> 00:04:47,537
We can definitely use this as evidence,

91
00:04:47,620 --> 00:04:49,414
but we still need a whistleblower

92
00:04:49,497 --> 00:04:52,959
to prove that Helena
Montoya is Red Dragon.

93
00:04:53,293 --> 00:04:54,711
Well, I have good news, Attorney.

94
00:04:55,169 --> 00:04:56,379
Just wait.

95
00:04:56,963 --> 00:04:58,673
I've got an ace up my sleeve.

96
00:05:05,221 --> 00:05:08,057
Well, I won't stay long.

97
00:05:08,141 --> 00:05:10,143
So, this is farewell for now.

98
00:05:11,811 --> 00:05:13,229
Are you sure…

99
00:05:14,188 --> 00:05:17,066
you don't want to come
back with me to the mansion?

100
00:05:17,442 --> 00:05:19,193
I really don't, Grandpa.

101
00:05:19,485 --> 00:05:20,570
My mission is here.

102
00:05:20,653 --> 00:05:22,363
But it was nice to see you again.

103
00:05:24,532 --> 00:05:25,700
Okay. I understand.

104
00:05:26,951 --> 00:05:28,244
Stay safe.

105
00:05:30,413 --> 00:05:32,540
Um, thank you. I'll be on my way.

106
00:05:40,423 --> 00:05:43,426
Uh… Grandpa, your Bible.

107
00:05:43,509 --> 00:05:44,677
You forgot it.

108
00:05:45,053 --> 00:05:46,054
[Julio chuckles]

109
00:05:47,638 --> 00:05:48,973
Did you know that…

110
00:05:52,268 --> 00:05:54,520
this Bible was from your grandmother?

111
00:05:57,231 --> 00:05:58,983
Right now, I'm thinking…

112
00:05:59,525 --> 00:06:02,195
it's better if I leave this to you.

113
00:06:03,821 --> 00:06:07,533
Think of it as a memento from her.

114
00:06:08,785 --> 00:06:09,786
[Arnaldo] Uh…

115
00:06:11,579 --> 00:06:14,332
-Okay.
-I'm sure she'd be happy.

116
00:06:15,833 --> 00:06:17,794
-All right, Grandpa.
-Take care, Arnaldo.

117
00:06:18,169 --> 00:06:19,587
-I'll go ahead.
-Okay.

118
00:06:20,379 --> 00:06:24,383
[sinister music playing]

119
00:06:47,031 --> 00:06:47,990
Yes, Madam?

120
00:06:48,074 --> 00:06:49,450
Call Mr. Yi.

121
00:06:49,992 --> 00:06:52,620
Tell him to expect the
shipment tomorrow evening.

122
00:06:52,954 --> 00:06:53,955
Yes.

123
00:06:54,497 --> 00:06:56,415
[tense music]

124
00:06:56,499 --> 00:06:57,834
[keys beep]

125
00:06:57,917 --> 00:06:59,043
Crap!

126
00:07:00,378 --> 00:07:01,379
What's wrong?

127
00:07:02,588 --> 00:07:03,756
I'm sorry, Madam.

128
00:07:04,507 --> 00:07:06,717
My phone just keeps blacking out.

129
00:07:07,426 --> 00:07:08,928
Since when?

130
00:07:09,637 --> 00:07:10,888
This morning.

131
00:07:14,976 --> 00:07:16,018
Give me your phone.

132
00:07:23,901 --> 00:07:27,405
[sighs] You know, when
your phone blacks out,

133
00:07:27,488 --> 00:07:29,949
it means it's been cloned.

134
00:07:30,950 --> 00:07:31,993
That's impossible, Madam.

135
00:07:32,076 --> 00:07:34,162
Because I always have it with me.

136
00:07:34,245 --> 00:07:35,246
Shut up!

137
00:07:36,414 --> 00:07:38,249
Your phone has been cloned!

138
00:07:39,208 --> 00:07:40,209
[phone clatters]

139
00:07:46,674 --> 00:07:48,176
Get Romulo!

140
00:08:06,027 --> 00:08:08,321
[ominous music playing]

141
00:08:12,241 --> 00:08:13,868
"Then you will know the truth

142
00:08:13,951 --> 00:08:16,287
and the truth will set you free."

143
00:08:22,043 --> 00:08:24,962
[ominous music continues playing]

144
00:08:42,772 --> 00:08:44,482
I'll go to Myla at the safe house

145
00:08:44,565 --> 00:08:48,194
and ask her if she knows
the name Helena Montoya.

146
00:08:49,320 --> 00:08:52,615
Maybe she can help us find
even more evidence.

147
00:08:54,575 --> 00:08:56,619
-Don't leave my daughter.
-Yes, ma'am.

148
00:08:57,787 --> 00:08:58,788
Take care, dear.

149
00:08:59,997 --> 00:09:01,624
Get the car ready.

150
00:09:09,715 --> 00:09:11,551
Lily's pushing through
with the investigation?

151
00:09:12,969 --> 00:09:14,262
That's how she is.

152
00:09:15,096 --> 00:09:17,765
A little rain won't stop her.

153
00:09:18,140 --> 00:09:20,226
Camia, she's got a big storm coming.

154
00:09:20,309 --> 00:09:22,144
And my daughter is ready for that.

155
00:09:22,728 --> 00:09:24,855
Have you seen her bodyguards?

156
00:09:25,398 --> 00:09:27,733
A light breeze could blow them over.

157
00:09:28,693 --> 00:09:30,861
They're not ready for
Red Dragon's typhoon.

158
00:09:30,945 --> 00:09:34,031
My daughter doesn't need them, Damian.

159
00:09:34,574 --> 00:09:35,866
She's a fighter on her own.

160
00:09:35,950 --> 00:09:39,370
Those bodyguards are only
there to make me feel better.

161
00:09:39,453 --> 00:09:42,832
I trust that my daughter
is ready for what she's facing.

162
00:09:44,083 --> 00:09:45,876
I wish you would too.

163
00:09:47,295 --> 00:09:50,006
Especially if you want to be
a part of our family.

164
00:10:02,935 --> 00:10:03,978
[Romulo] Madam…

165
00:10:04,061 --> 00:10:06,022
this is the dark web's latest technology.

166
00:10:06,731 --> 00:10:08,941
We traced the IMEI number of

167
00:10:09,025 --> 00:10:10,860
whoever tapped Mercedes' phone.

168
00:10:11,861 --> 00:10:12,945
And?

169
00:10:14,155 --> 00:10:15,406
She was right.

170
00:10:16,282 --> 00:10:17,825
The one behind all this…

171
00:10:18,826 --> 00:10:19,869
is Lily Cruz.

172
00:10:21,495 --> 00:10:23,998
[breathes heavily]

173
00:10:24,457 --> 00:10:27,585
[tense music playing]

174
00:10:36,469 --> 00:10:40,723
[phone ringing]

175
00:10:42,350 --> 00:10:43,351
Hello?

176
00:10:45,978 --> 00:10:48,648
What? How did that happen?

177
00:10:49,940 --> 00:10:52,151
All right. I'll deal with it.

178
00:10:54,403 --> 00:10:55,821
Lily needs to know about this.

179
00:11:01,118 --> 00:11:02,411
[Emilia] Hi, Mama!

180
00:11:02,912 --> 00:11:05,539
I bought you some scarves.
I did some shopping today.

181
00:11:05,623 --> 00:11:06,499
Hello!

182
00:11:11,212 --> 00:11:13,714
I can see you're busy. I should leave now.

183
00:11:13,798 --> 00:11:14,924
-Sorry.
-No.

184
00:11:15,007 --> 00:11:17,718
Just stay here, Emilia. Sit beside me.

185
00:11:18,177 --> 00:11:19,220
Oh, okay.

186
00:11:20,721 --> 00:11:21,847
What happened?

187
00:11:28,813 --> 00:11:32,566
I just realized
that I'm allergic to flowers.

188
00:11:33,943 --> 00:11:36,529
Lilies, in particular.

189
00:11:36,904 --> 00:11:39,031
[tense music continues playing]

190
00:11:52,878 --> 00:11:55,131
Lily, where's the cellphone I gave you?

191
00:11:55,923 --> 00:11:57,216
It's here. Have a seat.

192
00:11:59,552 --> 00:12:00,719
Why?

193
00:12:00,970 --> 00:12:02,805
My source said they traced the phone.

194
00:12:02,888 --> 00:12:04,223
So you need to give it to me.

195
00:12:05,474 --> 00:12:07,893
If that's true, then that means…

196
00:12:09,061 --> 00:12:12,565
Red Dragon already knows
that we cloned their phone.

197
00:12:13,023 --> 00:12:15,526
Probably. That's why I need
to dispose of it.

198
00:12:16,026 --> 00:12:17,027
No need, Jepoy.

199
00:12:17,903 --> 00:12:20,406
I'm sure Red Dragon already knows

200
00:12:20,489 --> 00:12:22,158
that I'm her enemy.

201
00:12:35,045 --> 00:12:38,257
[ominous music playing]

202
00:12:47,558 --> 00:12:50,561
[unsettling music playing]

203
00:13:41,403 --> 00:13:44,490
[unsettling music playing]

204
00:14:31,203 --> 00:14:32,454
[Diego] Arnaldo?

205
00:14:33,873 --> 00:14:34,874
Arnaldo!

206
00:14:40,337 --> 00:14:41,338
Arnaldo!

207
00:14:45,759 --> 00:14:46,760
Arnaldo.

208
00:14:51,807 --> 00:14:52,808
Are you okay?

209
00:14:54,768 --> 00:14:57,354
I think I'm committing a sin against God.

210
00:14:58,689 --> 00:14:59,940
What do you mean?

211
00:15:04,028 --> 00:15:05,237
Well…

212
00:15:05,988 --> 00:15:08,032
I've been having some thoughts lately.

213
00:15:09,950 --> 00:15:10,951
About a woman.

214
00:15:13,037 --> 00:15:15,789
I don't know if it's all just a dream, or…

215
00:15:16,665 --> 00:15:20,544
if it's a fragment of my memories.

216
00:15:22,546 --> 00:15:24,006
Well, what do you see?

217
00:15:26,383 --> 00:15:28,719
[sighs] Bad things.

218
00:15:29,803 --> 00:15:30,846
I feel things…

219
00:15:32,932 --> 00:15:34,308
Lustful things toward her.

220
00:15:42,733 --> 00:15:45,527
[tense music playing]

221
00:15:56,080 --> 00:15:57,957
For the life of me, I don't know…

222
00:15:59,416 --> 00:16:01,877
why I see her that way.

223
00:16:03,504 --> 00:16:06,465
And, I know she's
a friend of yours, Diego.

224
00:16:07,925 --> 00:16:09,009
So, I hope you can forgive me

225
00:16:09,093 --> 00:16:12,388
for thinking such things about her.

226
00:16:13,347 --> 00:16:15,015
I hope you don't hate me for it.

227
00:16:17,101 --> 00:16:18,185
I don't hate you.

228
00:16:22,481 --> 00:16:25,234
But, I think I should keep this for now.

229
00:16:26,443 --> 00:16:29,947
Yeah. Maybe that'll make
the bad dreams go away.

230
00:16:32,783 --> 00:16:34,159
Where did you get this, by the way?

231
00:16:34,702 --> 00:16:36,662
I found it inside the Bible
Grandpa gave me.

232
00:16:36,745 --> 00:16:39,415
[suspenseful music]

233
00:16:50,092 --> 00:16:51,844
[Helena] I can't allow my true identity

234
00:16:51,927 --> 00:16:53,721
to be exposed to the public.

235
00:16:54,888 --> 00:16:56,807
My empire…

236
00:16:57,349 --> 00:17:00,102
the empire that I've worked so hard for

237
00:17:00,185 --> 00:17:04,189
is going to crumble the moment
people find out who I really am.

238
00:17:05,441 --> 00:17:07,109
And that's the problem, Mama.

239
00:17:07,484 --> 00:17:08,986
Good old Lily Cruz.

240
00:17:09,069 --> 00:17:11,155
She's like a mosquito.

241
00:17:11,447 --> 00:17:14,074
She'll keep coming back
no matter what you do,

242
00:17:14,158 --> 00:17:15,701
just to suck your precious blood dry.

243
00:17:15,784 --> 00:17:17,786
[tense music]

244
00:17:18,287 --> 00:17:22,583
There's only one way to kill
those pesky mosquitoes.

245
00:17:23,584 --> 00:17:24,835
By crushing them!

246
00:17:26,003 --> 00:17:28,047
Love it, Mama! [giggles]

247
00:17:32,176 --> 00:17:35,345
[phone ringing]

248
00:17:36,430 --> 00:17:39,349
-[phone ringing]
-[Helena scoffs]

249
00:17:39,433 --> 00:17:41,477
Speaking of the mosquito.

250
00:17:41,560 --> 00:17:43,937
-I think she actually heard us.
-[phone ringing]

251
00:17:46,231 --> 00:17:49,276
[phone ringing]

252
00:17:50,944 --> 00:17:52,988
Beautiful morning, Lily!

253
00:17:53,072 --> 00:17:55,157
Not as beautiful as you are, Mama.

254
00:17:55,866 --> 00:17:58,577
To what do I owe the
pleasure of this call?

255
00:17:59,411 --> 00:18:00,370
<i>Um…</i>

256
00:18:00,454 --> 00:18:03,123
Well, I missed you, so I was thinking…

257
00:18:03,707 --> 00:18:06,627
-lunch?
-[Helena laughs]

258
00:18:06,710 --> 00:18:09,755
My, what a coincidence!

259
00:18:09,838 --> 00:18:13,926
I was just thinking
of the exact same thing.

260
00:18:14,927 --> 00:18:16,220
<i>Oh, really, Mama?</i>

261
00:18:17,304 --> 00:18:19,223
So… See you.

262
00:18:30,734 --> 00:18:31,693
Julio!

263
00:18:33,487 --> 00:18:35,948
[Julio] Psst! Don't.

264
00:18:37,950 --> 00:18:39,576
It's okay. Leave us for a while.

265
00:18:39,660 --> 00:18:41,620
We'll just talk.

266
00:18:42,162 --> 00:18:44,289
He won't hurt me. He's a good boy.

267
00:18:46,542 --> 00:18:47,751
Diego…

268
00:18:48,043 --> 00:18:50,003
I'm afraid today is just not your day.

269
00:18:50,462 --> 00:18:53,298
I don't have any spare
change left to give you.

270
00:18:53,841 --> 00:18:54,967
[tuts] Sorry.

271
00:18:55,509 --> 00:18:56,802
What's all this about?

272
00:18:59,805 --> 00:19:02,141
Do you even care for Arnaldo?

273
00:19:03,308 --> 00:19:04,977
More than my life.

274
00:19:06,228 --> 00:19:08,397
If that's true, don't ruin his new life.

275
00:19:09,106 --> 00:19:11,358
Don't deprive him of his happiness!

276
00:19:12,151 --> 00:19:14,695
Ooh… Happiness, you say?

277
00:19:15,779 --> 00:19:17,281
Whose happiness?

278
00:19:19,283 --> 00:19:20,450
Yours?

279
00:19:21,410 --> 00:19:22,494
Or…

280
00:19:23,287 --> 00:19:26,540
Lily Cruz's?

281
00:19:27,958 --> 00:19:29,084
Diego…

282
00:19:37,259 --> 00:19:38,260
[scoffs]

283
00:19:39,428 --> 00:19:41,013
I know Arnaldo well.

284
00:19:42,556 --> 00:19:45,934
He won't be too happy when he finds out

285
00:19:46,018 --> 00:19:48,896
what you've been doing to him.

286
00:19:50,689 --> 00:19:53,192
So, don't go lecturing me…

287
00:19:53,817 --> 00:19:55,736
about Arnaldo's happiness.

288
00:19:58,947 --> 00:20:01,533
Don't you dare come near my brother again.

289
00:20:05,454 --> 00:20:07,039
Why are you furious?

290
00:20:09,124 --> 00:20:11,919
Is it because…

291
00:20:13,587 --> 00:20:16,548
Arnaldo is slowly starting to remember…

292
00:20:17,799 --> 00:20:20,719
Ivy Aguas?

293
00:20:27,017 --> 00:20:28,560
Ivy Aguas is dead.

294
00:20:30,938 --> 00:20:32,648
Both she…

295
00:20:34,274 --> 00:20:35,692
and the old Arnaldo!

296
00:20:40,030 --> 00:20:41,448
Stay away from my brother!

297
00:20:43,867 --> 00:20:44,993
[laughs]

298
00:20:45,869 --> 00:20:48,914
The ghosts are haunting you, Diego.

299
00:20:48,997 --> 00:20:50,707
[laughs viciously]

300
00:20:52,084 --> 00:20:54,044
They're running after you.

301
00:20:59,424 --> 00:21:00,425
Hmm.

302
00:21:04,638 --> 00:21:06,223
That bastard…

303
00:21:06,848 --> 00:21:10,978
has been crossing me for far too long!

304
00:21:13,230 --> 00:21:14,982
[Julio] <i>You idiot!</i>

305
00:21:15,899 --> 00:21:17,985
<i>Go ahead, Grandpa.</i>

306
00:21:18,068 --> 00:21:20,362
<i>I'm not the same kid you used</i>
<i>to abuse. You can't scare me.</i>

307
00:21:20,737 --> 00:21:22,781
[Julio] <i>Who do you think you are?</i>

308
00:21:22,864 --> 00:21:24,283
<i>I raised you!</i>

309
00:21:24,366 --> 00:21:26,618
<i>I fed you and sent you to school.</i>

310
00:21:26,702 --> 00:21:30,914
<i>I'm ashamed to even call you an Ardiente.</i>

311
00:21:31,206 --> 00:21:32,708
[Diego] <i>Julio, your time is up.</i>

312
00:21:32,791 --> 00:21:34,918
<i>Because I'll make sure that</i>
<i>from this day on,</i>

313
00:21:35,002 --> 00:21:37,713
<i>evil will no longer reign in Ardiente.</i>

314
00:21:37,796 --> 00:21:39,214
<i>Julio Ardiente…</i>

315
00:21:39,298 --> 00:21:40,799
<i>-is a cheater!</i>
<i>-Mr. Torillo, why are you here?</i>

316
00:21:40,882 --> 00:21:42,384
[Diego] <i>We are here to protest against</i>

317
00:21:42,467 --> 00:21:45,262
<i>Julio Ardiente's proclamation</i>
<i>as governor of this province!</i>

318
00:21:45,345 --> 00:21:48,140
<i>Julio Ardiente!</i>
<i>I believe this is your money.</i>

319
00:21:48,223 --> 00:21:51,018
<i>The money you used</i>
<i>to bribe Secretary Martel!</i>

320
00:21:51,351 --> 00:21:52,894
<i>And who do we have here?!</i>

321
00:21:52,978 --> 00:21:54,563
<i>You just can't accept defeat, can you?</i>

322
00:21:54,646 --> 00:21:55,480
<i>You only won…</i>

323
00:21:55,564 --> 00:21:57,190
<i>-Sir!</i>
<i>-…because you cheated!</i>

324
00:21:57,274 --> 00:21:58,692
<i>As long as I'm alive,</i>

325
00:21:58,775 --> 00:22:01,361
<i>you'll never be the</i>
<i>governor of this province.</i>

326
00:22:02,529 --> 00:22:03,572
<i>Remember that!</i>

327
00:22:03,864 --> 00:22:05,866
<i>Do you even care for Arnaldo?</i>

328
00:22:05,949 --> 00:22:07,576
<i>Don't ruin his new life.</i>

329
00:22:07,826 --> 00:22:08,910
<i>Stay away from my brother!</i>

330
00:22:10,954 --> 00:22:11,955
Colonel.

331
00:22:16,251 --> 00:22:21,089
I want you to kill Diego Torillo now!

332
00:22:38,190 --> 00:22:39,274
Jepoy?

333
00:22:40,108 --> 00:22:41,276
What are you doing?

334
00:22:41,526 --> 00:22:42,736
Where's Lily?

335
00:22:44,112 --> 00:22:45,864
She's still at Mister Pandoy's
birthday party.

336
00:22:45,947 --> 00:22:47,616
-Aren't you going?
-I forgot!

337
00:22:50,202 --> 00:22:52,704
I'll just catch up. I should go now.

338
00:22:53,622 --> 00:22:54,706
Jepoy, wait.

339
00:22:56,666 --> 00:23:00,170
Thanks for helping Lily expose Red Dragon.

340
00:23:03,090 --> 00:23:04,925
That's my role, Anna.

341
00:23:07,010 --> 00:23:08,637
To protect you and Lily.

342
00:23:09,096 --> 00:23:11,473
And be a true friend.

343
00:23:14,434 --> 00:23:15,435
Thanks.

344
00:23:15,977 --> 00:23:17,312
I hope…

345
00:23:17,979 --> 00:23:19,272
that doesn't change.

346
00:23:19,356 --> 00:23:22,526
[soft music playing]

347
00:23:22,609 --> 00:23:24,778
Everything changes, Anna.

348
00:23:34,704 --> 00:23:35,664
Doesn't it?

349
00:23:35,747 --> 00:23:38,375
[soft music continues playing]

350
00:23:51,138 --> 00:23:55,475
[phone ringing]

351
00:23:56,726 --> 00:23:57,727
Hello?

352
00:23:59,312 --> 00:24:01,857
Okay, I'm on my way. Bye.

353
00:24:03,024 --> 00:24:04,317
Jepoy, I have to go.

354
00:24:19,374 --> 00:24:20,375
[sighs]

355
00:24:21,751 --> 00:24:22,752
[exhales]

356
00:24:25,380 --> 00:24:28,425
It should be simple, right?

357
00:24:29,509 --> 00:24:30,844
All I want

358
00:24:31,344 --> 00:24:34,306
is for Diego Torillo to die!

359
00:24:35,390 --> 00:24:36,433
Yes, sir.

360
00:24:36,516 --> 00:24:38,143
Once you've done it,

361
00:24:39,060 --> 00:24:41,396
bring me his corpse

362
00:24:41,479 --> 00:24:42,814
as proof

363
00:24:43,815 --> 00:24:45,775
that you did it successfully.

364
00:24:47,360 --> 00:24:48,403
Yes, sir.

365
00:24:49,654 --> 00:24:50,906
Colonel.

366
00:24:53,074 --> 00:24:54,910
This is how it's going to go down.

367
00:24:56,369 --> 00:25:00,749
Diego Torillo takes his last breath

368
00:25:00,832 --> 00:25:01,917
by sunset.

369
00:25:03,251 --> 00:25:07,297
Or you just might not see
another sunrise in your life.

370
00:25:07,380 --> 00:25:09,049
Am I clear?

371
00:25:09,132 --> 00:25:11,509
-Yes, sir.
-Go.

372
00:25:22,187 --> 00:25:25,315
-My, Loring, that's a lot!
-Of course.

373
00:25:25,398 --> 00:25:27,317
-We're expecting visitors.
-[Lily] Miss Loring!

374
00:25:27,400 --> 00:25:29,194
-See? They're here.
-It's Lily!

375
00:25:29,277 --> 00:25:30,153
Lily!

376
00:25:30,237 --> 00:25:31,112
-Mr. Pandoy!
-Nanny! Uncle!

377
00:25:31,196 --> 00:25:32,405
Lily! Diego, son.

378
00:25:32,489 --> 00:25:34,241
-Happy, happy birthday!
-Oh, my! Thank you.

379
00:25:34,324 --> 00:25:37,160
-There we go.
-I'm so happy you visited us.

380
00:25:37,244 --> 00:25:39,120
Of course, Mr. Pandoy.

381
00:25:39,204 --> 00:25:41,539
-I wouldn't miss your birthday.
-[Pandoy chuckles]

382
00:25:41,623 --> 00:25:44,209
I heard you cooked
a lot yesterday, Miss Loring.

383
00:25:44,292 --> 00:25:46,169
I'm sorry I couldn't come.

384
00:25:46,253 --> 00:25:49,506
-It's okay. Diego ate it all.
-[Loring laughs]

385
00:25:49,589 --> 00:25:51,132
He still has grease on his lips. [laughs]

386
00:25:51,216 --> 00:25:53,760
[Loring] Yeah. He licked everything clean.

387
00:25:53,843 --> 00:25:56,930
I almost put the dishes away
without washing them.

388
00:25:57,013 --> 00:25:58,848
Hang on, I'm innocent over here.

389
00:25:59,140 --> 00:26:01,601
And it's Uncle's birthday.
Shine the spotlight on him.

390
00:26:01,685 --> 00:26:03,311
-Me?
-That's right!

391
00:26:04,104 --> 00:26:05,105
-Well, since it's…
-Oh, my.

392
00:26:05,188 --> 00:26:06,273
-Mr. Pandoy's birthday…
-What's all that?

393
00:26:06,356 --> 00:26:07,399
Hold on. Wait.

394
00:26:07,482 --> 00:26:08,900
[Pandoy] That's a lot!

395
00:26:08,984 --> 00:26:11,278
-Are they all for me?
-Yes. And these too.

396
00:26:11,361 --> 00:26:12,612
-Wow!
-This one's from my mom…

397
00:26:12,696 --> 00:26:14,572
-This is a lot!
-These are from Anna and Jepoy.

398
00:26:14,656 --> 00:26:16,658
-I'm very grateful. Thank you.
-Wow!

399
00:26:16,950 --> 00:26:17,951
-Oh!
-Oh.

400
00:26:18,034 --> 00:26:21,246
Diego, Jepoy… [chuckles]

401
00:26:21,329 --> 00:26:22,622
These are so nice.

402
00:26:22,706 --> 00:26:24,374
-There's more, Nanny.
-Oh, this is such a cute box!

403
00:26:24,457 --> 00:26:26,376
-Look at this!
-I bet that's expensive.

404
00:26:26,459 --> 00:26:27,669
-You think so?
-It's probably a ring…

405
00:26:27,752 --> 00:26:30,255
-Let's see.
-…a necklace, or a bracelet.

406
00:26:30,338 --> 00:26:31,548
[Loring] Surprise!

407
00:26:32,590 --> 00:26:35,051
Ooh. Who's this from?

408
00:26:36,303 --> 00:26:37,345
[Diego] It's…

409
00:26:37,637 --> 00:26:38,638
from Arnaldo.

410
00:26:38,930 --> 00:26:41,391
[tense music playing]

411
00:26:41,891 --> 00:26:43,018
That demon.

412
00:26:45,937 --> 00:26:46,980
I'm sorry…

413
00:26:47,439 --> 00:26:51,860
but we won't accept gifts
from a known murderer.

414
00:26:51,943 --> 00:26:52,944
Give it back.

415
00:26:53,903 --> 00:26:54,946
Come on, Nanny.

416
00:26:57,365 --> 00:27:00,702
Nanny, Uncle, my brother has changed.

417
00:27:01,661 --> 00:27:03,288
Maybe we could give him a chance.

418
00:27:04,497 --> 00:27:06,249
Why? Have you already forgotten?

419
00:27:06,333 --> 00:27:10,253
He's the reason why your
Uncle Pandoy almost died!

420
00:27:10,337 --> 00:27:11,296
[Pandoy scoffs]

421
00:27:16,801 --> 00:27:18,678
I haven't forgotten that.

422
00:27:18,762 --> 00:27:20,972
Then, I hope you understand

423
00:27:21,056 --> 00:27:24,559
why we can't do what you're asking for.

424
00:27:25,602 --> 00:27:28,355
I'm aware that your brother's still sick.

425
00:27:28,855 --> 00:27:32,859
But just because he's forgotten
all the crimes he did to us…

426
00:27:33,485 --> 00:27:36,571
doesn't mean we can just forget

427
00:27:36,654 --> 00:27:39,616
all the pain and suffering
he put us through.

428
00:27:39,699 --> 00:27:41,284
He didn't just scratch the surface,

429
00:27:41,368 --> 00:27:42,952
he went and cut us all deep.

430
00:27:47,457 --> 00:27:49,542
I just want all of us to get along.

431
00:27:52,670 --> 00:27:54,297
-Excuse me.
-Diego--

432
00:27:55,882 --> 00:27:57,050
[Pandoy sighs heavily]

433
00:27:57,509 --> 00:27:59,636
[sighs heavily] Sorry, Lily.

434
00:28:00,470 --> 00:28:01,471
Uh…

435
00:28:02,472 --> 00:28:03,681
No worries, Mr. Pandoy.

436
00:28:04,766 --> 00:28:06,935
I understand how you feel.

437
00:28:07,018 --> 00:28:08,061
[Pandoy sighs heavily]

438
00:28:08,144 --> 00:28:09,771
I'll talk to him.

439
00:28:12,941 --> 00:28:13,942
[Pandoy exhales]

440
00:28:20,198 --> 00:28:21,241
Diego!

441
00:28:23,034 --> 00:28:24,536
Diego, wait.

442
00:28:26,079 --> 00:28:27,997
Come on, let's go back.

443
00:28:29,249 --> 00:28:30,458
I'll just stay here awhile.

444
00:28:32,794 --> 00:28:36,714
Diego, just try to understand
Miss Loring and Mr. Pandoy.

445
00:28:37,382 --> 00:28:39,008
I do understand them.

446
00:28:40,135 --> 00:28:42,846
It's just that I want
all of us to get along.

447
00:28:43,596 --> 00:28:45,974
That's the best thing for everyone.

448
00:28:46,057 --> 00:28:48,143
I understand that.

449
00:28:48,977 --> 00:28:51,187
And yes, Arnaldo is your brother.

450
00:28:52,230 --> 00:28:54,482
But it's not that easy to forget

451
00:28:54,566 --> 00:28:56,735
the pain your brother caused.

452
00:29:01,781 --> 00:29:02,866
[Anna] Okay, kids. That's it…

453
00:29:02,949 --> 00:29:04,826
-for today's storytelling.
-[guitar riffs]

454
00:29:04,909 --> 00:29:06,411
[Anna] Let's continue tomorrow, okay?

455
00:29:06,745 --> 00:29:08,788
[girl] One more story, Teacher Anna.

456
00:29:08,872 --> 00:29:10,373
-Please.
-You go ahead.

457
00:29:10,457 --> 00:29:11,750
You go on ahead.

458
00:29:13,418 --> 00:29:16,546
No, you go back there because
it's Mr. Pandoy's birthday.

459
00:29:19,090 --> 00:29:20,216
I'll be right with you.

460
00:29:21,593 --> 00:29:22,594
[Diego] Really.

461
00:29:26,890 --> 00:29:28,141
Go on ahead.

462
00:29:28,224 --> 00:29:32,020
[sad music playing]

463
00:29:40,153 --> 00:29:44,324
[Anna] Why don't you kids
listen to Arnaldo for now, okay?

464
00:29:44,783 --> 00:29:46,242
[boy] Yes, ma'am. Come on!

465
00:29:46,326 --> 00:29:49,704
[guitar riffs]

466
00:29:49,788 --> 00:29:51,915
[Arnaldo] Oh! [giggles]

467
00:29:51,998 --> 00:29:53,166
Wanna hear a song?

468
00:29:54,417 --> 00:29:55,418
[Arnaldo] Let's see…

469
00:29:59,422 --> 00:30:00,423
Go on.

470
00:30:04,844 --> 00:30:05,720
Hold on…

471
00:30:11,518 --> 00:30:14,521
-Can we go play by the river?
-Just a sec, um…

472
00:30:14,604 --> 00:30:17,023
-Please, Arnaldo?
-Please!

473
00:30:17,106 --> 00:30:18,858
[girl] Over there!

474
00:30:19,484 --> 00:30:20,944
Um, all right. All right.

475
00:30:21,569 --> 00:30:22,779
[girl] Let's go!

476
00:30:24,781 --> 00:30:25,782
Sure, let's go!

477
00:30:26,241 --> 00:30:27,242
[girl] Let's go.

478
00:30:35,875 --> 00:30:37,877
You wanna talk about what's bothering you?

479
00:30:41,297 --> 00:30:42,549
It's not like I've forgotten

480
00:30:42,632 --> 00:30:44,509
about all the things Arnaldo did.

481
00:30:45,009 --> 00:30:46,261
But he's changed.

482
00:30:46,344 --> 00:30:47,595
You've seen it too, right?

483
00:30:47,679 --> 00:30:49,430
He's a new man!

484
00:30:50,849 --> 00:30:54,185
But you still can't force
everyone else to forgive him.

485
00:30:54,936 --> 00:30:57,355
To them, he's still the same old Arnaldo.

486
00:30:57,939 --> 00:31:00,066
The one who hurt them,
the one who abused them.

487
00:31:01,025 --> 00:31:03,403
The one who killed Nanny Carlotta.

488
00:31:04,946 --> 00:31:05,989
So, you too, huh?

489
00:31:08,199 --> 00:31:09,868
You can't forgive him either?

490
00:31:11,119 --> 00:31:14,622
At first, it was really hard
for me to forgive Arnaldo.

491
00:31:15,915 --> 00:31:18,877
He killed the kindest person
I'd ever met in my entire life.

492
00:31:19,919 --> 00:31:21,421
And I just couldn't forget that

493
00:31:21,504 --> 00:31:23,506
whenever I saw him.

494
00:31:25,341 --> 00:31:29,345
But you and Lily helped me
let that grudge go.

495
00:31:30,471 --> 00:31:33,558
And, the more I see him now,

496
00:31:34,267 --> 00:31:37,937
the less I remember
all the bad things he's done.

497
00:31:39,814 --> 00:31:42,233
It's like this Arnaldo is someone else.

498
00:31:43,610 --> 00:31:46,696
So, do the same thing
for Miss Loring and Mr. Pandoy.

499
00:31:47,530 --> 00:31:51,242
Help them forget all those
horrible things about Arnaldo.

500
00:31:53,870 --> 00:31:54,954
Don't worry.

501
00:31:55,580 --> 00:31:57,790
Jepoy and I are here for you.

502
00:31:59,292 --> 00:32:00,627
You know that, right?

503
00:32:01,628 --> 00:32:05,632
[soft music playing]

504
00:32:43,169 --> 00:32:44,170
Eat up.

505
00:32:45,797 --> 00:32:48,800
[sentimental music playing]

506
00:32:51,886 --> 00:32:52,887
[Pandoy exhales]

507
00:32:59,018 --> 00:32:59,978
Uh…

508
00:33:02,021 --> 00:33:03,106
Come here, Diego.

509
00:33:05,024 --> 00:33:06,651
We're sorry about what happened earlier.

510
00:33:10,571 --> 00:33:11,948
Now, come on. Join us.

511
00:33:12,865 --> 00:33:13,866
Sit.

512
00:33:16,452 --> 00:33:17,495
Eat with us.

513
00:33:19,122 --> 00:33:20,289
[Diego] No, it's not that.

514
00:33:22,125 --> 00:33:24,002
I should be the one apologizing.

515
00:33:25,795 --> 00:33:28,214
Uncle, Nanny, I'm sorry.

516
00:33:28,297 --> 00:33:29,882
I let my emotions get the better of me.

517
00:33:32,468 --> 00:33:33,761
I wasn't thinking…

518
00:33:34,470 --> 00:33:36,681
about all the horrible
things Arnaldo did to you.

519
00:33:38,641 --> 00:33:40,977
But, I'm going to prove to you…

520
00:33:41,310 --> 00:33:43,187
that my brother really has changed.

521
00:33:44,147 --> 00:33:46,232
So, I'm begging you, please…

522
00:33:46,941 --> 00:33:48,776
give him another chance.

523
00:33:49,861 --> 00:33:53,114
He needs our help and our support.

524
00:34:02,415 --> 00:34:04,208
-[Pandoy sighs]
-We'll try, Diego. For you.

525
00:34:08,379 --> 00:34:10,339
Oh, my. [sighs heavily]

526
00:34:10,423 --> 00:34:11,549
Now, hold on.

527
00:34:12,550 --> 00:34:13,885
It's a birthday party, right?

528
00:34:14,135 --> 00:34:15,428
Enough with the drama.

529
00:34:15,511 --> 00:34:17,138
-[Pandoy laughs]
-We should be happy.

530
00:34:17,221 --> 00:34:19,057
Well, I know I wasn't being dramatic.

531
00:34:19,140 --> 00:34:20,975
-It's a party!
-Food makes everything better.

532
00:34:21,059 --> 00:34:24,520
-All I need is this.
-But, of course!

533
00:34:24,604 --> 00:34:25,563
Fritters!

534
00:34:25,646 --> 00:34:27,356
There's more where that came from.

535
00:34:27,440 --> 00:34:29,275
-Don't forget the ice cream!
-It's great.

536
00:34:29,358 --> 00:34:30,693
[Loring and Pandoy giggle]

537
00:34:30,777 --> 00:34:31,819
-But wait--
-Pile it up high.

538
00:34:31,903 --> 00:34:33,571
-You can have it all!
-It's not the ice cream.

539
00:34:33,654 --> 00:34:34,906
I think something's missing.

540
00:34:34,989 --> 00:34:37,492
-What?
-Hold on, give me a minute…

541
00:34:37,575 --> 00:34:38,785
-What is it?
-We're not missing anything.

542
00:34:38,868 --> 00:34:39,952
Be right back. Don't move, okay?

543
00:34:40,036 --> 00:34:40,953
I'll just go get something.

544
00:34:41,037 --> 00:34:42,246
-Where are you going?
-Wait.

545
00:34:42,330 --> 00:34:43,331
Hey!

546
00:34:43,706 --> 00:34:45,041
-Where's he going?
-Don't move, okay?

547
00:34:45,124 --> 00:34:48,002
I'll just go get something.

548
00:34:48,086 --> 00:34:49,962
-But, your food--
-Wait here.

549
00:34:50,046 --> 00:34:51,422
[laughing] Where's he going?

550
00:34:51,506 --> 00:34:53,466
[laughing]

551
00:34:54,509 --> 00:34:56,385
What do we do?

552
00:34:56,469 --> 00:34:59,430
-Anyway…
-Happy birthday!

553
00:34:59,514 --> 00:35:01,891
-Thank you.
-Once more.

554
00:35:02,725 --> 00:35:05,103
[in sweet voice] Happy birthday to you.

555
00:35:06,687 --> 00:35:08,898
[in silly voice] Whoops, maybe tomorrow.

556
00:35:09,190 --> 00:35:10,733
[Pandoy laughing] Hey!

557
00:35:10,817 --> 00:35:12,443
It won't be my birthday by then.

558
00:35:12,527 --> 00:35:13,528
Okay, fine. Here.

559
00:35:13,611 --> 00:35:15,988
-No, thanks.
-Oh, stop sulking!

560
00:35:20,535 --> 00:35:23,246
You're going on a
lunch date with Lily Cruz?

561
00:35:23,329 --> 00:35:24,580
I wanna watch!

562
00:35:24,664 --> 00:35:27,083
I wanna watch how you crush that woman.

563
00:35:28,251 --> 00:35:29,085
I'm sorry, Emilia.

564
00:35:29,168 --> 00:35:32,004
-But… no.
-But, Mama, I wanna go.

565
00:35:32,088 --> 00:35:35,842
I wanna check whether or not
she really is indestructible.

566
00:35:36,050 --> 00:35:38,344
I want you to stay and watch.

567
00:35:38,845 --> 00:35:39,971
But, Mama…

568
00:35:40,054 --> 00:35:42,640
I can take her out on my own.

569
00:35:42,723 --> 00:35:43,933
Let me handle her.

570
00:35:44,267 --> 00:35:45,726
[Emilia sighs] Mama…

571
00:35:45,810 --> 00:35:46,769
Emilia…

572
00:35:47,019 --> 00:35:48,479
for once…

573
00:35:49,147 --> 00:35:51,190
you need to stay behind.

574
00:35:51,899 --> 00:35:54,819
You get too emotional
when Lily Cruz is around.

575
00:35:55,778 --> 00:35:58,614
You need a solid presence of mind.

576
00:35:59,031 --> 00:36:01,742
You have to be 10 steps
ahead of your enemy.

577
00:36:02,952 --> 00:36:06,622
And emotions will only get in the way.

578
00:36:07,206 --> 00:36:08,791
So, you have to stay and watch.

579
00:36:09,834 --> 00:36:11,169
Okay, Mama.

580
00:36:11,252 --> 00:36:13,588
I will watch how the queen works.

581
00:36:13,671 --> 00:36:14,922
Exactly.

582
00:36:22,471 --> 00:36:27,560
[explosions]

583
00:36:28,769 --> 00:36:32,023
[Lily] <i>You're the one who</i>
<i>blew up the media complex!</i>

584
00:36:32,106 --> 00:36:32,982
[Myla] <i>That's right!</i>

585
00:36:35,693 --> 00:36:36,986
<i>Where's Madam Red Dragon?</i>

586
00:36:37,820 --> 00:36:38,696
<i>You just missed her.</i>

587
00:36:39,989 --> 00:36:41,657
<i>Do you know what this is?</i>

588
00:36:41,741 --> 00:36:43,034
[Lily] <i>Ouch!</i>

589
00:36:43,951 --> 00:36:45,411
<i>It could be painful.</i>

590
00:36:45,494 --> 00:36:47,538
<i>It could be deadly.</i>

591
00:36:49,916 --> 00:36:52,710
[tense music playing]

592
00:36:59,342 --> 00:37:03,512
<i>I'm done playing pretend, Helena Montoya.</i>

593
00:37:03,596 --> 00:37:04,972
<i>So now,</i>

594
00:37:05,056 --> 00:37:09,018
<i>I'm going to make sure</i>
<i>you admit it yourself.</i>

595
00:37:09,101 --> 00:37:11,646
<i>You are none other than Red Dragon.</i>

596
00:37:21,447 --> 00:37:23,950
-Where's Diego?
-He left.

597
00:37:28,704 --> 00:37:30,331
Those are some big catfish.

598
00:37:30,998 --> 00:37:32,124
Well, I caught them.

599
00:37:33,084 --> 00:37:34,585
Unlike Diego's.

600
00:37:34,669 --> 00:37:38,965
[sweet music playing]

601
00:37:39,590 --> 00:37:41,801
So, why did he drop by?

602
00:37:42,635 --> 00:37:45,972
He had a fight with
Miss Loring and Mr. Pandoy.

603
00:37:47,098 --> 00:37:51,018
That's their problem. What's with the hug?

604
00:37:52,687 --> 00:37:55,231
I gave him advice, and he felt better,

605
00:37:55,314 --> 00:37:56,524
so he hugged me.

606
00:37:57,650 --> 00:37:59,193
You seem happy about it.

607
00:38:00,152 --> 00:38:02,196
So what if I'm happy?

608
00:38:02,280 --> 00:38:03,656
Are you jealous?

609
00:38:06,492 --> 00:38:08,369
Yes, I am. Is that a problem?

610
00:38:10,329 --> 00:38:12,123
I'm jealous because I don't just like you,

611
00:38:12,206 --> 00:38:15,418
I really like you too, Anna.

612
00:38:16,085 --> 00:38:17,878
I don't know what to do.

613
00:38:17,962 --> 00:38:20,464
You're always in my head and in my heart.

614
00:38:23,301 --> 00:38:25,803
Jepoy, I'm not the one in your heart.

615
00:38:27,179 --> 00:38:28,306
It's always been Lily,

616
00:38:29,181 --> 00:38:31,892
ever since we were kids.

617
00:38:32,977 --> 00:38:35,980
I just pretended to
be Lily, but I'm not her.

618
00:38:36,522 --> 00:38:38,774
In case you forgot, Jepoy,

619
00:38:39,150 --> 00:38:41,360
you almost gave your life for her.

620
00:38:41,444 --> 00:38:42,903
I haven't forgotten, Anna.

621
00:38:43,863 --> 00:38:46,490
I know you're not Lily.

622
00:38:46,907 --> 00:38:48,659
But it's all clear to me now, Anna.

623
00:38:50,119 --> 00:38:53,164
The only reason I did
what they told me was

624
00:38:53,247 --> 00:38:56,208
because of my debt of gratitude
towards her and Miss Prianka.

625
00:38:57,918 --> 00:38:58,961
But now…

626
00:39:00,379 --> 00:39:01,380
I--

627
00:39:01,464 --> 00:39:02,757
I don't know what's happening.

628
00:39:02,840 --> 00:39:06,761
I don't owe you anything, but…

629
00:39:06,844 --> 00:39:09,388
I don't know why I'm
feeling these things for you.

630
00:39:10,890 --> 00:39:13,642
[Jepoy scoffs] You know what? I give up.

631
00:39:15,394 --> 00:39:20,024
Because of what happened,
I told Natalie to stay away.

632
00:39:20,107 --> 00:39:22,526
If only I'd known that…

633
00:39:24,028 --> 00:39:25,154
If only I'd known what?

634
00:39:27,073 --> 00:39:29,033
That I had no place in your heart.

635
00:39:29,116 --> 00:39:32,703
[upbeat music playing]

636
00:39:32,787 --> 00:39:35,289
Thanks to Diego.
What does he have that I don't?

637
00:39:42,088 --> 00:39:45,174
Jepoy, Diego is important to me
because he's my friend.

638
00:39:46,509 --> 00:39:48,969
And that's that. It won't change.

639
00:39:50,554 --> 00:39:51,806
It won't change, huh?

640
00:39:57,103 --> 00:39:58,104
How about me?

641
00:40:02,358 --> 00:40:03,984
Is there still room for me in there?

642
00:40:08,739 --> 00:40:11,158
You never left my heart, Jepoy.

643
00:40:14,578 --> 00:40:16,205
[stutters] Really?

644
00:40:19,875 --> 00:40:20,876
[giggles]

645
00:40:22,294 --> 00:40:23,295
Really?

646
00:40:27,883 --> 00:40:29,093
Maybe we should eat.

647
00:40:30,970 --> 00:40:31,887
Sounds good.

648
00:40:31,971 --> 00:40:34,765
[upbeat music playing]

649
00:40:43,899 --> 00:40:44,900
Have a seat.

650
00:41:02,960 --> 00:41:05,504
-[phone ringing]
-[laughing]

651
00:41:05,588 --> 00:41:08,299
-Silly old cow.
-[phone ringing]

652
00:41:09,717 --> 00:41:11,969
-Julio.
-<i>Helena</i>.

653
00:41:12,303 --> 00:41:15,264
I'm touched. You have my number.

654
00:41:15,806 --> 00:41:16,807
<i>Why?</i>

655
00:41:16,891 --> 00:41:19,727
I even know your address.
Your number is nothing.

656
00:41:19,810 --> 00:41:22,271
What about you? How did you get my number?

657
00:41:22,354 --> 00:41:24,940
I have my ways.

658
00:41:25,232 --> 00:41:27,276
Hmm. Stalker, much?

659
00:41:27,359 --> 00:41:28,777
[laughs]

660
00:41:30,029 --> 00:41:33,532
I can sense by the quiver in your voice…

661
00:41:34,533 --> 00:41:37,578
that you're tickled
pink just talking to me.

662
00:41:38,037 --> 00:41:38,954
[Julio laughs]

663
00:41:39,038 --> 00:41:40,039
Oh, yeah.

664
00:41:40,331 --> 00:41:42,917
I'm very excited about my lunch date.

665
00:41:44,168 --> 00:41:47,087
Ooh. Someone I know?

666
00:41:48,214 --> 00:41:49,256
Julio…

667
00:41:49,340 --> 00:41:52,760
is that a tinge of jealousy that I hear?

668
00:41:53,677 --> 00:41:55,054
Not really.

669
00:41:56,263 --> 00:41:59,308
I also have someone coming over tonight.

670
00:42:00,518 --> 00:42:01,519
Oh, really?

671
00:42:02,102 --> 00:42:03,354
What are you serving?

672
00:42:04,146 --> 00:42:05,356
I don't know yet.

673
00:42:06,482 --> 00:42:08,192
But it's something…

674
00:42:08,275 --> 00:42:09,610
bloody.

675
00:42:09,693 --> 00:42:11,529
[chuckles]

676
00:42:12,029 --> 00:42:13,697
Just how we like it.

677
00:42:14,532 --> 00:42:17,076
Yes, just the way we like it.

678
00:42:17,910 --> 00:42:19,370
[Helena laughs]

679
00:42:19,453 --> 00:42:21,247
Be seeing you, Helena.

680
00:42:27,503 --> 00:42:28,712
[laughs]

681
00:42:30,005 --> 00:42:31,549
Damn, Helena,

682
00:42:31,632 --> 00:42:35,678
I know you're still head
over heels in love with me.

683
00:42:36,971 --> 00:42:38,931
I can read you like a book.

684
00:42:41,016 --> 00:42:42,059
You…

685
00:42:42,560 --> 00:42:44,645
you're so good-looking,

686
00:42:45,229 --> 00:42:46,397
you're unbelievable.

687
00:42:47,481 --> 00:42:50,234
[laughing]

688
00:42:52,236 --> 00:42:54,071
Oh, this is going to be fun.

689
00:43:06,000 --> 00:43:08,210
I'll get back at you, Diego Torillo.

690
00:43:21,765 --> 00:43:23,434
[action music playing]

691
00:43:30,524 --> 00:43:31,775
[Helena] Bring that inside.

692
00:43:31,859 --> 00:43:33,152
Our guest is coming.

693
00:43:51,920 --> 00:43:55,924
[sinister music playing]

694
00:44:26,413 --> 00:44:29,416
[action music playing]

695
00:44:43,681 --> 00:44:44,682
Lily!

696
00:44:45,474 --> 00:44:46,600
Baby girl!

697
00:44:46,684 --> 00:44:49,228
-Welcome to my home.
-Mama!

698
00:44:50,437 --> 00:44:52,815
Mama, thanks for having me.

699
00:44:52,898 --> 00:44:54,358
Of course!

700
00:44:55,109 --> 00:44:56,235
I brought wine.

701
00:44:56,318 --> 00:44:59,613
I did my research and found out
that this one's your favorite.

702
00:44:59,696 --> 00:45:00,989
Excellent!

703
00:45:01,532 --> 00:45:02,699
[eerie music]

704
00:45:08,497 --> 00:45:09,456
Let's go in!

705
00:45:09,540 --> 00:45:10,666
-Of course. Let's go.
-Come.

706
00:45:12,876 --> 00:45:14,753
Oh. Excuse me.

707
00:45:16,046 --> 00:45:17,464
For girls only.

708
00:45:17,548 --> 00:45:18,549
Lily…

709
00:45:19,550 --> 00:45:22,386
Lily, I've invited you to my home.

710
00:45:22,469 --> 00:45:24,805
It seems like you don't trust me.

711
00:45:26,682 --> 00:45:27,766
[chuckles]

712
00:45:27,850 --> 00:45:29,560
Of course, I do, Mama.

713
00:45:31,103 --> 00:45:32,771
Kindly wait outside.

714
00:45:34,690 --> 00:45:36,650
-Happy?
-Of course!

715
00:45:36,942 --> 00:45:38,944
How are we supposed to have girl talk

716
00:45:39,027 --> 00:45:41,155
in the presence of your bodyguards?

717
00:45:41,238 --> 00:45:42,281
[Lily chuckles]

718
00:45:43,157 --> 00:45:45,659
Wow, Mama, your house is so big!

719
00:45:46,160 --> 00:45:48,287
It's like a dragon's lair.

720
00:45:50,789 --> 00:45:52,458
-It's huge.
-[Helena chuckles]

721
00:45:55,377 --> 00:45:56,879
Lily, please come in.

722
00:45:57,296 --> 00:45:59,548
Really, Mama, your house is so big.

723
00:45:59,631 --> 00:46:01,884
Doesn't it scare you…

724
00:46:01,967 --> 00:46:03,594
[Lily on TV screen]
<i>…or make you feel lonely?</i>

725
00:46:03,677 --> 00:46:05,762
[Helena] <i>No. Not at all. </i>[chuckles]

726
00:46:05,846 --> 00:46:07,723
<i>You must be so hungry. Please sit down.</i>

727
00:46:17,733 --> 00:46:18,692
You may go.

728
00:46:19,902 --> 00:46:21,528
Oh… [giggles]

729
00:46:21,612 --> 00:46:23,238
I hope you like this!

730
00:46:23,530 --> 00:46:25,949
Well, it looks delicious! So, let's eat?

731
00:46:26,033 --> 00:46:27,159
Let's.

732
00:46:27,576 --> 00:46:30,954
[suspenseful music playing]

733
00:46:39,713 --> 00:46:41,006
Mmm…

734
00:46:44,968 --> 00:46:45,928
Mm!

735
00:46:47,429 --> 00:46:48,680
Wow, Mama.

736
00:46:49,223 --> 00:46:51,600
-The fish tastes amazing.
-[Helena chuckles]

737
00:46:52,726 --> 00:46:54,269
It's not fish.

738
00:46:56,438 --> 00:46:57,564
Um…

739
00:46:57,648 --> 00:47:00,275
If it's not fish, what is it?

740
00:47:03,278 --> 00:47:04,363
It's snake.

741
00:47:07,074 --> 00:47:09,451
[laughing]

742
00:47:23,382 --> 00:47:24,633
[phone ringing]

743
00:47:27,094 --> 00:47:28,303
Hello, Nanny.

744
00:47:30,722 --> 00:47:33,767
Diego… Are you on your way back?

745
00:47:33,850 --> 00:47:35,310
Yes, Nanny. I'm headed home.

746
00:47:35,394 --> 00:47:38,063
Nanny… Don't tell Uncle Pandoy this, okay?

747
00:47:38,146 --> 00:47:39,690
But I bought him his favorite cake.

748
00:47:40,274 --> 00:47:42,025
<i>Just wait for me, okay?</i>

749
00:47:43,694 --> 00:47:47,531
[stutters] Okay. Just… Hurry home.

750
00:47:47,614 --> 00:47:50,033
I'm almost there.
I'll be there in no time.

751
00:47:50,826 --> 00:47:52,536
[tense music playing]

752
00:47:54,204 --> 00:47:55,205
[Loring] All right.

753
00:47:59,668 --> 00:48:02,129
[tense music continues playing]

754
00:48:18,395 --> 00:48:20,522
<i>You have to refrain</i>
<i>from calling me "Mama."</i>

755
00:48:20,606 --> 00:48:22,608
<i>I'll call you by your first name.</i>

756
00:48:22,691 --> 00:48:23,692
<i>Just call me Helena.</i>

757
00:48:23,775 --> 00:48:26,278
<i>No, maybe I can call you, um…</i>

758
00:48:26,361 --> 00:48:27,404
<i>Hel.</i>

759
00:48:27,904 --> 00:48:29,656
[Jose] <i>We're all set, sir.</i>

760
00:48:29,740 --> 00:48:31,908
<i>We're just waiting for Diego.</i>

761
00:48:31,992 --> 00:48:34,328
[Helena] <i>They say you're indestructible.</i>

762
00:48:34,411 --> 00:48:36,371
<i>I have nothing to hide from you now.</i>

763
00:48:36,455 --> 00:48:39,541
<i>An eye for an eye, Red Dragon.</i>

764
00:48:41,001 --> 00:48:43,003
<i>-What will you do to Diego?</i>
<i>-Diego.</i>

765
00:48:43,837 --> 00:48:45,672
<i>-Stop resisting!</i>
-[Diego screams]

766
00:48:45,756 --> 00:48:46,715
<i>Give me your gun!</i>

767
00:48:46,798 --> 00:48:48,592
-[Loring] <i>Not Diego!</i>
-[gunshot]

768
00:48:48,675 --> 00:48:49,635
[distorted screams]

769
00:48:50,761 --> 00:48:53,472
[theme music playing]
